    "body": "### Problem\n\n\nEditing a ts file in a large project can make neovim unresponsive with a minimal configuration and tsc LSP client (7.0.2). \nEach emitted `textDocument/didChange` currently triggers immediate refreshes\nfor both:\n\n1. `textDocument/diagnostic`\n2. `textDocument/semanticTokens/full`\n\nIt seems neovim cancels stale requests and sends replacements immediately. \nWith native TypeScript, cancellation is cooperative: requests that have reached its queue or started a project update can continue consuming server resources after `$/cancelRequest`. \nDuring continuous typing, this creates queued obsolete language-service work instead of applying backpressure.\n\n## Observed behavior\n\nI tried on my work project to import something from a dependency, similar to:\n```ts\nimport {} from 'effect/unstable/▌'\n```\nand my computer was slowing down, the autocomplete takes some time to render, multiple \"Loading: Project 'tsconfig.json'\" or \"Loading\" are being printed in the statusline.\n\n\n\nOver roughly 12 seconds of editing one TypeScript file, the LSP log contained:\n\n| Item | Count |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Incremental `didChange` notifications | 24 |\n| Individual incremental edits | 45 |\n| Pull diagnostic requests | 25 |\n| Semantic full-token requests | 23 |\n| Client cancellation notifications | 44 |\n| Document-highlight requests | 0 |\n| TypeScript project/program updates | 22 |\n\nThe replacement text across the edits totaled only 42 bytes, so this is not caused by large full-buffer synchronization.\n\nOne semantic-token request was cancelled on the next edit, but the server did not acknowledge cancellation for 10.208 seconds. \nThe server reported several `RequestedLanguageService (pending file changes)` project updates, including:\n\n| Duration |\n| ---: |\n| 2.635 s |\n| 1.258 s |\n| 1.221 s |\n| 1.193 s |\n| 349 ms |\n| 108 ms |\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\n```lua\n// while typing the import statement, i can see the logs from the LspProgress appear multiple times like if the tsc was initializing again and again, making ram and cpu increase a lot and slowing down everything\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"LspProgress\", {\n\tgroup = vim.api.nvim_create_augroup(\"LspProgress\", { clear = true }),\n\tcallback = function()\n\t\tvim.notify(vim.lsp.status(), vim.log.levels.INFO, { id = \"lsp_progress\", title = \"LSP Progress\" })\n\tend,\n})\n\nlocal pattern = 'typescript'\nlocal cmd = { 'tsc', '--lsp', '--stdio' }\nlocal root_markers = {\n  'package-lock.json',\n  'yarn.lock',\n  'pnpm-lock.yaml',\n  'bun.lockb',\n  'bun.lock',\n  '.git',\n}\n\nlocal settings = vim.empty_dict()\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\n  pattern = pattern,\n  callback = function(args)\n    local match = vim.fs.find(root_markers, { path = args.file, upward = true })[1]\n    local root_dir = match and vim.fn.fnamemodify(match, ':p:h') or nil\n    vim.lsp.start({\n      name = 'bugged-ls',\n      cmd = cmd,\n      root_dir = root_dir,\n      settings = settings,\n    })\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.diagnostic.config({ virtual_text = true })\n```\n\n\n1. Configure nvim with the minimal Lua configuration above.\n2. Open a ts file in a \"large project\" (tried to recreate a reproduction but it's too complex to recreate a project i have at work).\n3. Enable LSP debug logging with `:lua vim.lsp.log.set_level('debug')`.\n4. Type an import statement. (`import {} from 'effect/unstable|` with LspProgress autocommand you should see it pop a few times and the cpu/ram usage increase a lot)\n5. Observe many `didChange` notifications and a diagnostic/token replacement pair after each change flush.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNvim to remain responsive while typing, including when editing an import statement in this project. \nCPU and memory use should not continually increase during a typing burst, and diagnostics and semantic highlighting\nshould catch up shortly after I pause.\nThe log ideally would not show a growing amount of work for document versions that have already been superseded by newer edits.\n\n\nI don't believe this is a typescript issue as with helix using the same tsc binary I don't have any similar issue.\n\nI can understand this is quite hard to reproduce as the project needs to be quite large, I tried to create one with dummy data and so on but I could not replicate the same bug.\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1433+g61df463c5e\n\n### Language server name/version\n\ntsc 7.0.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nMacOS Tahoe 26.5.2 (25F84)\n\n### Log file\n\nhttps://gist.github.com/bpingris/18cb33f632eb24f1e5f07654601c99af",
