        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "some updates:\nafter some more digging on comparing the lsp logs of neovim and helix, and also their source code with the help of a LLM (gpt5.6 terra) I found a configuration that seems to fix these slowdowns:\nit was indeed the `debounce text changes` setting **and** disabling the semantic tokens feature\n```lua\nvim.lsp.config('tsc', {\n  -- existing tsc configuration\n\n  flags = {\n    debounce_text_changes = 500,\n  },\n\n  on_init = function(client)\n    vim.lsp.semantic_tokens.enable(false, { client_id = client.id })\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nHelix does local tree-sitter syntax highlighting and does not request LSP semantic tokens\n\nSo i guess we could either have a default value for the debounce in the tsc configuration on the neovim lspconfig repository? \nand what about the semantic tokens feature? is it required if we have treesitter already doing the \"same\" job (if i understand correctly what semantic tokens does).\n\nFWIW, here's the helix different debounce values:\n- automatic completion: 250 ms\n- completion after an LSP trigger character: 5 ms\n- pull diagnostics after edits: 250 ms\n- cross-file diagnostic refresh: 1 second",
            "created_at": "2026-08-31T16:41:36Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41521#issuecomment-5481443830",
