        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Semantic tokens are much more accurate than treesitter (especially for hard-to-parse languages like c++ that actually _need_ semantic analysis for certain expressions). It shouldn't be disabled by default in nvim-lspconfig.\n\nI just looked at this a bit though. tsc is a thin wrapper around tsserver which is not a true LSP server. It's LSP-ish, but there have been a number of issues and complaints with the performance of this LSP in particular because it doesn't natively talk LSP. That's likely why it doesn't support cancellation or semantic tokens delta requests. Apparently VS Code devs asked the typescript devs a long time ago to support delta semantic token requests and it just never happened.\n\nIn your case, the solution is to probably disable this feature for tsc since it's just not performant server-side. \n\nWere you still using my branch when testing those changes to debounce and disable semantic token highlighting?\n\n",
